# oracle: w313gm_lj_tail — w246gm_lj_gibbs (T 1.2, 3 translations, 1 exchange, 3 volume moves per cycle) with pair_modify tail yes: the tail correction is the pair style's from its last init or reinit (an insertion and an accepted deletion leave it at the old counts, a rejected exchange recomputes it), and pressure is printed for the tail pressure
# oracle-partitions: 2
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 4.9e-14, atoms 1.3e-14. The exchanges accepted at steps 36 and 44 leave the tail correction at the old atom count in the printed pe and press (with a tail recomputed after every change, step 44 differs from native by 4e-2).
variable temp index 2.0
variable ntranslate index 3
variable nexchange index 1
variable nvolume index 3
variable displace index 0.5
variable max_dlogvolratio index 0.5
variable nsteps index 60
units lj
atom_style atomic
variable rho world 0.05 0.6
variable ncell world 1 2
lattice fcc ${rho}
region box block 0 ${ncell} 0 ${ncell} 0 ${ncell}
create_box 1 box
create_atoms 1 box
mass 1 1.0
pair_style lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff 1 1 1.0 1.0 2.5
pair_modify tail yes
neighbor 0.3 bin
neigh_modify every 1 delay 5 check yes
fix 2 all gemc 1 ${ntranslate} ${nexchange} ${nvolume} ${temp} ${displace} ${max_dlogvolratio} 29494
thermo 1
thermo_style custom step pe press vol atoms
thermo_modify format float %.15g
run ${nsteps}
